\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Stronger As US Jobs Data Boosts Copper Prices\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 18:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended stronger versus the dollar Friday, erasing earlier losses, after stronger-than-expeced U.S. payrolls data boosted copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The peso gained to CLP467.80 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP468.40, while trading in a wide range of CLP465.00 to CLP471.50.\par \par \uc2 On the back of concerns about global growth, the peso had tracked international copper prices lower in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 The surprisingly strong U.S. jobs report, however, boosted international copper prices and commodities-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's largest copper producer, accounting for a third of global output, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often takes direction from the industrial metal's prices abroad.\par \par \uc2 Also, as Chile's economy is highly export-intensive and almost a third of its exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso mostly brushed off the euro's slide against major rivals, including the dollar, on speculation that Greece could leave the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Although Greek officials dismissed the speculation, "the euro took a beating nonetheless. It's surprising that the peso didn't weaken on that, but rising copper prices probably served to counteract the euro's dive," said a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader, who asked not to be named.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of the its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million on Friday at an average rate of CLP470.02. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.35 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher as softer-than-expected consumer price index data, will likely lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the pace of interest rates hikes next week to 25 basis points.\par \par \uc2 The CPI grew 0.3% in April from the previous month, the government statistics institute reported earlier in the session, lower than the 0.4% increase participants were expecting.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.62%, from 2.57% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.90%, versus 2.87% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 06-05-11 1655GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110506e756001es\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
