\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cbank maintains  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  pace\b0\par\par\uc2 156 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2011\par 21:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, May 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it would continue with daily purchases of $50 million in U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , keeping the pace of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for 2011 aimed at taming the strong peso.\par \par \uc2 The fresh monthly batch of daily dollar purchases are set to run from May 9 to June 8.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL>, which weakened sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began in early January, has since clawed back nearly all of the 7 percent initially lost due to strong prices for the nation's main export copper and wider dollar weakness. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week hit a three-year high.\par \par \uc2 Economic authorities have said capital controls are not the solution, and markets are watching to see what additional measures the state or \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take. [ID:nN26270395] [ID:nN26276247]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Santiago Newsroom)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CENBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110509e756001t1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
