\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher, Led By Transport, Power Generators\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 481 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2011\par 21:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index closed higher Thursday, boosted by transportation and power generation companies on falling international crude-oil prices, while market attention focused on the first initial public offering of shares this year.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa rose 0.6% to 4788.35 points, while market volume surged to 272.5 billion Chilean pesos ($581.7 million), down from CLP89.5 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Trading in specialty branded generic drugs manufacturer Recalcine (CFR.SN), which raised nearly $370 million through its IPO, accounted for 70% of the session's market volume. Recalcine rose to CLP98.00 after selling 2.03 billion shares at CLP85 each.\par \par \uc2 Also, shares of transportation companies jumped as tumbling crude-oil futures pointed to the prospect of lower transportation costs.\par \par \uc2 Flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) gained 3.1% to CLP13,200.00, while shipping company Vapores (VAPORES.SN) grew 1.7% to CLP366.00.\par \par \uc2 Power generation companies, whose costs will fall on lower crude-oil and diesel prices, also gained.\par \par \uc2 Generator E-CL (ECL.SN), formerly known as Edelnor, jumped 4.5% to CLP1,315.00 and energy holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) rose 1.7% to CLP201.50.\par \par \uc2 "Diesel prices fell sharply, boosting generators like E-CL, which have all of their installed capacity in thermal-generation", including coal, diesel and natural gas, said Cristian Jadue, analyst with local investment bank Santander GBM.\par \par \uc2 Pulp and wood products company CMPC (CMPC.SN) climbed 1.4% to CLP25,201.00 after its net profit jumped 78% on the year in the first quarter to $141.3 million.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended weaker versus the dollar, on institutional dollar buying as international copper prices plummeted and the euro sank against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to CLP468.40 to the dollar, distancing itself further from a recent three-year high, versus Wednesday's close of CLP465.50. The peso traded in a range of CLP467.20 to CLP469.40.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of the its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million on Thursday at an average rate of CLP467.81. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.30 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower as market consensus sees rising costs for bread will push the consumer price index higher.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.57% versus 2.60% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.87%, from 2.89% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 05-05-11 1923GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110505e7550017p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
