\par\par \b \uc2 IMF: Capital Controls Are Valid Tool, But Unnecessary In Chile\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2011\par 20:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Although capital controls are a valid tool, implementing them in Chile to fight back the peso's appreciation isn't warranted, Miguel Savastano, the deputy director of the Western Hemisphere Department of the International Monetary Fund, said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the peso has crawled back to a three-year high versus the dollar, having appreciated almost 8% since its low point this year and nearly 12% over the last 52 weeks.\par \par \uc2 While Chile attracts strong investment flows due to its robust economic growth and tightening monetary policy, the country also sees strong capital outflows, making it unnecessary to "impose more restrictions on capital," said Savastano at the Andean nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to the most recent data, Chile's private pension fund managers, or AFPs, which are the nation's largest institutional investors, held nearly 46% of their investments abroad.\par \par \uc2 Late last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to gradually increase the cap on AFP investments abroad to 80%, from its then 60% limit.\par \par \uc2 In recent months, the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jose De Gregorio, has repeated that there's no need to implement capital controls as Chile isn't seeing net capital inflows and will post a small surplus in its current account this year.\par \par \uc2 In the 1990s, Chile implemented capital controls, through a reserve requirement on foreign investments, which officials have said weren't effective in curbing speculative capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Also, despite the IMF's recent warning to the contrary, Savastano said that after the local stock market's fall this year, Chile wasn't currently facing a stock-market bubble.\par \par \uc2 By mid-February the local blue-chip Ipsa index had slipped over 13% compared to the closing price at the end of 2010. The Ipsa has since pared those losses and is 2.4% lower year-to-date.\par \par \uc2 If the stock market continues recovering, however, in "about six months or so, it's going to start showing symptoms again of being overvalued," Savastano said.\par \par \uc2 Late last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the Ipsa index was overpriced, fueling a quick sell-off.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 04-05-11 1818GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110504e7540019b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
