\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Lower As IMF Warns Of Stock-Market Bubbles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2011\par 21:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended lower Tuesday after a top official at the International Monetary Fund warned of stock-market bubbles in countries such as Argentina, Chile and Brazil.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa ended 0.3% lower at 4810.76 points, while market volume grew to 102.8 billion Chilean pesos ($223.1 million) from CLP74.8 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 "We are entering dangerous territory...there are signs of overvalued stocks in some countries," said Nicolas Eyzaguirre, director of the IMF's western-hemisphere department.\par \par \uc2 Also, the Ipsa fell as it tracked slumping U.S. markets. As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average, which recently slipped 38 points, or 0.3%, to 12771.\par \par \uc2 "There was a double effect today--the Ipsa followed U.S. markets lower and comments by the IMF served to further that effect," said Ximena Garcia, head of studies at local brokerage EuroAmerica, adding "I don't necessarily agree with the IMF's assessment."\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) declined 2.7% to CLP27,300.00, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) shed 1.3% to CLP12,848.00, and bank \uc2 Banco de Chile\uc2  (BCH, CHILE.SN) lost 1.6% to CLP67.01.\par \par \uc2 However, power generator \uc2 E-CL SA\uc2  (ECL.SN), formerly known as Edelnor, jumped 3.3% to CLP1,275.10 after the company said it seeks to export natural gas from the Mejillones regasification plant to Argentina. The company also said it plans to sell its power-transmission assets in the longer term and concentrate on its core power-generation business.\par \par \uc2 Also, telecommunications operator Entel (ENTEL.SN) gained 2.3% to CLP9,266.30 after its first-quarter net profit rose 42% to CLP52.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso erased the tumble it saw in early trading to end stronger against the dollar, amid institutional investors' dollar sales and gains in international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed to CLP461.00 to the dollar, versus Monday's close of CLP462.40, after trading in a broad range of CLP461.00 to CLP464.70.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million Tuesday at an average rate of CLP463.74. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.2 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed following a regularly scheduled \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign-debt auction.\par \par \uc2 In addition, shorter-term bond yields rose following Scotiabank's Chile unit issuing $375 million in inflation-indexed five-year bonds. The bonds obtained a yield of 3.31% and a spread of 75 basis point over the corresponding \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.59% versus 2.56% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.87%, unchanged from the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Carolina 