\par\par \b \uc2 Chile's Peso Closes Weaker On Bin Laden Death, Profit Taking\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2011\par 18:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended weaker versus the dollar Monday, on the back of Osama bin Laden's death and profit taking as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at a three-year high.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to CLP462.40 to the dollar, versus Friday's close of CLP460.20. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a narrow range of CLP460.70 to CLP462.90.\par \par \uc2 The peso slumped against the dollar, as did most major rivals, after the U.S. reported it had killed Al Qaeda leader bin Laden.\par \par \uc2 "With the peso trading at a three-year high [versus the dollar], news of bin Laden's death sparked profit taking," said Osvaldo Molina, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with local brokerage and investment bank Larrain Vial.\par \par \uc2 Also, declining international copper prices helped to pull the peso lower. As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for nearly a third of global supply, the peso often takes trading cues from the metal's international prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of the its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program purchased $50 million on Monday at an average rate of CLP461.14. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.15 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed ahead of an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign debt scheduled for Tuesday. Also, participants awaited local bank Scotiabank's issue of $375-million in inflation-indexed five year bonds, also scheduled for Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended unchanged at 2.56%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.87%. from 2.86% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 02-05-11 1655GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110502e752000vx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
