\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Central Banker: Peso 3%-5% Firmer Without  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Paper\b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2011\par 20:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso, currently trading at three-year highs against the dollar, would likely be 3% to 5% stronger were it not for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, bank governor Rodrigo Vergara told Friday's La Segunda evening daily.\par \par \uc2 Vergara's view coincides with that of other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors and Finance Minister Felipe Larrain.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank's $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was sizable and generated significant expenses to the bank.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is costly because financing it is more expensive that the returns obtained on reserves," Vergara told the newspaper in an interview.\par \par \uc2 Vergara, who is seen as a candidate for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president when current chief Jose De Gregorio's term ends in December, said the bank wasn't likely to pick up the pace of its current purchases of $50 million a day.\par \par \uc2 As to capital controls, Vergara said he agreed with De Gregorio's opinion that these measures aren't effective at curbing inflows.\par \par \uc2 He said Chile isn't seeing massive capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "[Capital controls] are available and one can't ever rule them out, but the evidence regarding their effectiveness is debatable," Vergara told the newspaper.\par \par \uc2 In the 1990s, Chile implemented controls, through a reserve requirement on foreign investment, which De Gregorio and Larrain have often stated didn't stop inflows.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 29-04-11 1852GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110429e74t00159\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
