\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Closes Marginally Stronger, Hits Fresh 3-Year High\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 April 2011\par 19:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended marginally stronger versus the dollar Friday, hitting a fresh three-year high, as market participants don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will implement additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to CLP460.20 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP460.40. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a very narrow range of CLP459.00 to CLP460.75.\par \par \uc2 While a stronger peso cuts into the export sector's competitiveness abroad, on the domestic front it eases imported inflationary pressures as fuel and food import costs fall locally.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main concern right now is inflation, so we aren't expecting any new [\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] measures," said Gloria Soto, at local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader FXCM \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In early January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program and has been buying $50 million a day since then. As part of the program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Chile\uc2  on Friday purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP460.50. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accumulated $4.1 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the stronger peso gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  room to slow the pace of its rate hikes, traders and analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to firm in coming sessions if the dollar extends its losses abroad and the peso could test a significant psychological barrier at CLP455, traders said.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher as the market awaits the April consumer price index data to be released late next week.\par \par \uc2 Based on bond prices, the market sees the CPI gaining 0.4% on the month in April.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.56%, from 2.55% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.86%, from 2.84% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 29-04-11 1733GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110429e74t0014n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
