\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market Debt Strengthens Mildly;  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy and Anjali Cordeiro   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2011\par 21:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Emerging-market debt strengthened slightly Thursday, as investors continued to shift to riskier and higher-yielding assets.\par \par \uc2 Following the U.S. Federal Reserve's signal that its ultraloose policy stance will remain in play for the foreseeable future--along with strong global liquidity conditions--investors placed their bets on riskier assets, though a bit more selectively.\par \par \uc2 "Risk appetite is probably going to remain strong, and is sort of steady as she goes," said Win Thin, emerging-market strategist at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . But "markets are still being a little bit discerning in terms of the EM story."\par \par \uc2 The risk premium on the \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  Emerging Markets Bond Index Global tightened by 2 basis points to 302 basis points over Treasurys. In price terms, its index rose 0.37%.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw mixed performance. Skepticism about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies in Brazil and Turkey weighed on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Turkish lira lost ground, with the dollar up 0.56% to TRY1.5258 late Thursday, according to CQG. The country's inflation will show an upward trend in the short-term due to the late reflections of oil-price rises and base effects, Turkey's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in minutes from its monetary policy committee meeting in April.\par \par \uc2 Brown Brother Harriman's Thin attributed Thursday's weakness to "some market concerns with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  credibility" and worries about unconventional monetary policy in Turkey, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been avoiding raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 On the Embig, Turkey's spread slimmed by 2 basis points to 188 basis points over Treasurys, while its index rose 0.18%.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not fare well. Only the Hungarian forint was able to eke out clear gains, strengthening to HUF264.20 against the euro from HUF264.60 late Wednesday. On the Embig, Hungary's spread tightened by 5 basis points to 260 basis points over Treasurys, while its index rose 0.60%.\par \par \uc2 In Latin America, the Brazilian real underperformed other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Possible government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the monthly settlement of the Brazilian real and unclear signs provided by the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  communique unleashed negative sentiment against the real. The dollar was recently up 1.76% at BRL1.5865.\par \par \uc2 "Brazil has a little more credibility in general, but they're losing it" because they appear to be chasing the curve, Thin said.\par \par \uc2 On the Embig, Brazil's spread shed 4 basis points to 173 basis points over Treasurys, while its index rose 0.54%.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso hit a fresh three-year high versus the dollar at CLP460.70, despite an ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, on the back of dollar weakness. \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debt, however, weakened mildly, with its spread adding 3 basis points to 124 basis points over Treasurys. Its index rose just 0.10%.\par \par \uc2 Argentina and Venezuela were solid outperformers on the Embig. Argentina's spread tightened by 10 basis points to 556 basis points over Treasurys, and its index jumped 1.75%. Venezuela's spread shed 5 basis points to 1146 basis points, and its index climbed 0.91%.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decisions will dominate emerging markets on Friday. Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its policy rate by 25 basis points to 3.75%, and Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen either keeping rates on hold or hiking by 25 basis points, according to \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 . Mexico, meanwhile, will release the minutes from its most recent rate-setting meeting, as well as the second-quarter inflation report.\par \par \uc2 -By Erin McCarthy and Anjali Cordeiro, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 --Anthony Esposito and Rogerio Jelmayer contributed to this article. [ 28-04-11 1939GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110428e74s0020q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
