\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends At Fresh 3-Year High As Dollar Continues Slide\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2011\par 18:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended at a new three-year high versus the dollar Thursday, as the greenback continued its sliding against major rivals after Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke indicated the prior session the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is far from tightening monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to CLP460.70 to the dollar, versus Wednesday's close of CLP462.10. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP459.00 to CLP461.00.\par \par \uc2 Despite an ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the peso has pushed its way back to a three-year high as traders the world over have been selling the dollar in droves in recent weeks, sending the greenback to multi-year lows against most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also, expectations for Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase the benchmark rate another 50 basis points to 5% in May and high copper prices are also boosting the peso.\par \par \uc2 With dollar weakness abroad and more monetary tightening expected in Chile, "the peso could strengthen to CLP450 in the short-term," said Sebastian Momberg, trader with local bank BCI.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Felipe Larrain reiterated Thursday that the government is just as concerned as exporters about the peso's strength, stating the government won't implement capital controls to curb dollar inflows.\par \par \uc2 Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and the peso's strength eats away at exporters' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 Traders believe the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unlikely to implement new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures now to combat the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 "Although Larrain has raised the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, they have begun threatening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to avoid surprising markets. We expect that the peso needs to make further gains before they actually pull the trigger," \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP460.18. It has accumulated $4.05 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 (Peso quote provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 28-04-11 1647GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110428e74s001yo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
