\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks Close Lower As Corporate Earnings Fail To Excite\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 21:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended lower Wednesday as corporate earnings failed to excite investors.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa shed 0.3% to 4754.91 points, while market volume slipped to 88.0 billion Chilean pesos ($190.4 million), from CLP133.4 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Among companies which recently reported earnings, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) lost 1% to CLP12,822.00. Faced with soaring crude oil prices that push fuel costs higher, LAN's first quarter net profit of $97.2 million disappointed investors, while its Ebitda, or earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization, of $250.7 million beat them.\par \par \uc2 Also, the nation's largest power producer, \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN), fell 1.3% to CLP865.00, after its first quarter earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization fell 10.8% on the year to CLP201.37 billion.\par \par \uc2 Its parent company, power holding firm \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) declined 0.7% to CLP195.02 after its Ebitda slipped 15.5% on the year to CLP434.36 billion.\par \par \uc2 "In general the earnings reported weren't that exciting," said Rodrigo Arriagada, analyst with local brokerage Molina y Swett.\par \par \uc2 The local stock market shrugged off U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's statements that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy easing would remain steady after June and that there was no specific timeframe to begin tightening interest-rate policy, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Among other decliners fuel and forestry conglomerate Copec (COPEC.SN), the Ipsa's heaviest-weighted share, decreased 0.5% to CLP8,797.60 and chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) fell 1.4% to CLP26,817.00.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso strengthened slightly, ending at a fresh three-year high versus the dollar, as institutional investors sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP462.10 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP462.30. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP461.30 to CLP463.75.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP462.02. It has accumulated $4 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as participants anxiously awaited the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting and Chairman Ben Bernanke's first-ever post policy meeting press conference.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.53%, from 2.50% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.85%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 27-04-11 1935GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110427e74r001oz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
