\par\par \b \uc2 Chilean Peso Gains Slightly, Ends At Fresh 3-Year High\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 372 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2011\par 18:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso strengthened slightly Wednesday, ending at a fresh three-year high versus the dollar, as institutional investors sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP462.10 to the dollar, versus Tuesday's close of CLP462.30. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP461.30 to CLP463.75.\par \par \uc2 Despite falling international copper prices and the dollar's recovery against major rivals, the peso firmed on local greenback sales.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's premier copper producer, accounting for a third of global copper production and because nearly a third of the Andean nation's exports are bound for Europe, the peso often takes trading cues from international copper prices and the euro's movements versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso, however, pared back most of its gains during the session after Finance Minister Felipe Larrain told reporters the government will continue to monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and implement additional measures if these are needed.\par \par \uc2 "That verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rattled investors' nerves and helped to pull the peso back from its earlier highs," said Andrea Lombardi, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 Despite the peso's stubborn strength, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Jose De Gregorio reiterated earlier this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't implement capital controls since there isn't a net dollar inflow.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP462.02. It has accumulated $4.00 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as participants anxiously awaited the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting and Chairman Ben Bernanke's first-ever post policy meeting press conference later in the session.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.53%, from 2.50% on Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.85%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 27-04-11 1650GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110427e74r001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
