\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Real targets 12-yr high, Chilean peso jumps\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso hits 3-year high on cenbank comments\par \par \uc2 * Bets Fed will keep easy policy stance backs region\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso struggles against option barriers\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real firms 0.57 pct, Mexico peso up 0.28 pct\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds comments, changes dateline, previous SANTIAGO)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Jeb Blount\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, April 26 (Reuters) - Brazil's real neared its strongest level in 12 years on Tuesday and Chile's peso hit a three-year high on bets that policymakers would not step up their fight against further gains.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso jumped after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief was seen ruling out capital controls while Brazil's real gained on expectations \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  there would not deter more flows.\par \par \uc2 Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  benefited from bets that the U.S. Federal Reserve will signal its willingness to maintain cheap credit when it ends its policy-setting meeting on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Signs that U.S. rates will remain low through the year could push more investors to seek better returns in Latin America's higher yielding debt.\par \par \uc2 "As long as the Fed sustains low rates for a longer period, that allows Latin America to absorb more flows seeking higher yield," said Enrique Alvarez, head of Latin America research at IDEAglobal in New York.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso got a boost after the head of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled policymakers will not resort to capital controls to discourage flows. [ID:nN26270395] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on Chile peso: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qat29r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qat29r}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso <CLP=CL> bid 1.08 percent firmer at 462.30 per dollar, its strongest since May 2008. The peso erased the impact of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched in January.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Brazil have been trying to slow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains that hurt local manufacturers, but investors are betting policymakers will now allow further strengthening to help fight inflation from high commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 "This is hitting inflation expectations, and that has propelled central banks to be more tolerant with the exchange rate, which is seen less as an enemy these days as an ally," said Jimena Zuniga, an analyst at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Fed's ultra-loose monetary policy has pushed a tide of investment into Latin America. Brazil's current account deficit ballooned in March as the strong real boosted demand for foreign goods. [ID:nN26216964]\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real has surged nearly 8 percent since mid-March after the country's authorities were seen putting aside the threat of severe capital controls.\par \par \uc2 The real <BRBY> bid 0.57 percent firmer at 1.562 per dollar in the local spot market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is just off its strongest levels since it was allowed to float in early 1999.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was helped by expectations the government will have little success stemming the real's strength with less drastic measures such as taxes on short-term capital flows to Brazil and limits banks' short positions in dollars.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said movements in the futures market suggest investors think the government's latest measures will have little long-term impact.\par \par \uc2 The second dollar forward <DOLc2> on the BMFBovespa exchange, which reflects \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange expectations for May, fell 0.51 percent to 1.5695 reais to the dollar. By falling it shows market players are betting the real will strengthen more next month.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso <MXN=> firmed 0.28 percent to 11.5755 per dollar. Traders said major foreign banks were buying dollars to defend option positions around 11.57 per dollar and 11.55 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has gained more than 5 percent from a March intraday low to trade at its strongest in 2-1/2 years. The peso has recently hit levels stronger than many expected.\par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers have shown the least concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, which could spur even more bets on the peso.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting and writing by Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110429e74q0019b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
