\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2-Chile shuns capital controls, peso hits 3-yr peak\b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 18:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief says Chile not facing flood of capital\par \par \uc2 * His comments push peso to nearly three-year highs\par \par \uc2 * Chile likely to post a current account surplus in 2011\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments from De Gregorio, analyst, peso close)\par \par \uc2 By Brad Haynes and Moises Avila\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 26 (Reuters) - Chile's peso surged to three-year highs on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signaled it will not use capital controls to tame the rally, leading some in the market to bet it may ease the pace of rate hikes.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio reiterated that unlike some Latin American nations Chile was not facing dollar inflows that merit capital controls. He has repeatedly said the bank will prioritize its fight against inflation over taming the peso.\par \par \uc2 The peso <CLP=CL> jumped on his remarks, traders said, gaining 1 percent to bid 462.3 per dollar, firming past the 465.5 per dollar rate seen on Jan. 3, which triggered the launch of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has appreciated to its strongest level since April 2008 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has aggressively raised interest rates in recent months to fight inflation despite exporters' demands to do more to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking to college students about policies to tame \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength, De Gregorio said: "A more controversial tool is the use of capital controls, particularly in those countries that are seeing significant net capital inflows. However, this is not the case in Chile."\par \par \uc2 He said that Chile, the world's top copper producer, will likely post a current account surplus in 2011.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Felipe Larrain has said he is skeptical of capital controls and the government is not considering them.\par \par \uc2 Foreign bets on the Chilean peso's rally have also eroded the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, shifting sharply in recent weeks in favor of the peso. [ID:nN25208073]\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a TAKE A LOOK on Chile economy [ID:nN26HILEFI]\par \par \uc2 Chile peso evolution {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/qat29r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/qat29r}}}\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 BRAZILIAN MODERATION\par \par \uc2 "(De Gregorio) is clearly uncomfortable with these levels but does not have many options," said Matias Madrid, chief economist at Banco Penta.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe you could increase the monetary policy rate by 25 basis points rather than 50 or not even increase at the next meeting, if the bank feels a lot of pressure."\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark rate last week by 25 basis points rather than 50 in a split decision, backing off the intensity of monetary tightening and easing upward pressure on a rallying real <BRBY>. Brazil has also slapped taxes on some foreigners' investments to try to tame the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso is up around 18 percent against the dollar since mid 2010, outpacing the real's 15 percent gain. However year-to-date the real has gained 6 percent, while Chile's peso is broadly flat after erasing the 7 percent drop that followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's more moderate rate increase sparked market fears that authorities in Latin America's biggest economy are not doing enough to rein in inflation. Brazil's rate now stands at 12 percent, the highest among major economies. [ID:nN20289067]\par \par \uc2 Chile is also struggling with rising inflation as higher world oil and food prices pushed up consumer prices in March at the fastest pace in 18 months. [ID:nN08178268]\par \par \uc2 Joining emerging market peers from China to Peru, Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has responded by aggressively raising its benchmark rate. It has increased the rate by 100 basis points in the last two months to 4.5 percent, its highest in more than two years.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio and other members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board have not hinted at moderating the pace of rate hikes at their May 12 monetary policy meeting, but the bank's latest monthly poll of analysts forecast the rate at 4.75 percent next month.\par \par \uc2 In a sign that the bank may stick to hefty rate hikes, De Gregorio said in his speech that interest rate differentials between emerging markets and rich nations are not "astronomical" compared to the early 1990s.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Maria Jose Latorre; Writing by Alonso Soto; Editing by Simon Gardner and Kenneth Barry)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO (WRAPUP 2)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110429e74q0018c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
