\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso at pre- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  level near 3-yr high\b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 18:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso hit near three-year highs and returned to pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio on Tuesday reiterated the country was not facing dollar inflows that merit capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Following are analysts' reactions:\par \par \uc2 MATIAS MADRID, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT BANCO PENTA\par \par \uc2 "For the moment, there's not much you can do. Under 460 per dollar they will have to take some sort of measure, speed up the pace of daily dollar purchases if the peso hits 450 per dollar, capital controls ... there aren't many bullets left."\par \par \uc2 "At these levels, capital controls are completely ruled out, but they could opt for them if it reaches."\par \par \uc2 "He is clearly uncomfortable with these levels but does not have many options. Maybe you could increase the monetary policy rate by 25 basis points rather than 50 or not even increase at the next meeting, if the bank feels very under pressure."\par \par \uc2 NATHAN PINCHEIRA, ECONOMIST AT BANCHILE\par \par \uc2 "The tools the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has are extremely limited. The only real option is to increase the amount of daily dollar purchases, but it can only do that from May 6, when there is a new purchase calendar for the month."\par \par \uc2 "This level of exchange rate works on two levels. On the one hand it limits external inflation because the transfer to the exchange rate by fuels, for example, is lower, but that can also stoke demand, which brings secondary effects, which is precisely what it does not want."\par \par \uc2 "It could smooth the cycle of rising interest rates to 25 basis points instead of 50 bps. I don't think it's a question of holding them at this point, as it would be a very odd signal to the market given high inflation expectations for this year."\par \par \uc2 FLAVIA CATTAN-NASLAUSKY, \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST WITH RBS\par \par \uc2 "This is a catch-up rally, in the sense that the peso has been an underperformer until last week. This week we had a reinforcement of the weak dollar view, which means no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is left out."\par \par \uc2 "The question is do we go lower (firmer). This is a pretty significant level."\par \par \uc2 "We could go lower still a bit because of the positioning (peso foreign bets) and overall rally triggered by the dollar"\par \par \uc2 PEDRO TUESTA, ECONOMIST WITH 4CAST\par \par \uc2 "At this level (of the peso), markets will seek signals from the government before advancing further."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Maria Jose Latorre and Alonso Soto)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (INSTANT VIEW)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110429e74q0018b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
