\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Breaks Pre- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Level, Ends At 3-Year High\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2011\par 18:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--After breaching pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended 1.1% stronger Tuesday at a three-year high versus the dollar, buoyed by broad greenback weakness and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments that capital controls aren't needed.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP462.30 to the dollar, a level not seen since April 2008, versus Monday's close of CLP467.40. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP462.30 to CLP467.95.\par \par \uc2 Broad dollar weakness, as the U.S. Federal Reserve lags behind its major counter parts in increasing interest rates, has fueled the peso's strength, despite the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against its major rivals, with the dollar index sliding to its lowest level since August 2008, as participants expected the Federal Reserve to maintain loose monetary policy as the rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee begins a two-day meeting.\par \par \uc2 Also, earlier in the day, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Jose De Gregorio, speaking to university students, said Chile did not require capital controls as it is not seeing net capital inflows and will post a small surplus in its current account this year.\par \par \uc2 "With the dollar falling abroad and following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comments regarding capital control's, the peso broke a firm level of resistance and firmed beyond pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels," said Rodrigo Sarria, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with investment bank Celfin Capital.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president also said that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world are seeing an adjustment, in part due to the weak dollar, noting that such an adjustment was to be expected and contributed to alleviating international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions.\par \par \uc2 "There's no \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war going on, it's just \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  having a temper tantrum," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program in early January to beat back the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength and help exporters' competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP467.66 Monday. It has accumulated $3.95 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher as participants continue to await the outcome of the Fed's policy meeting and Chairman Ben Bernanke's first-ever post policy meeting press conference later in the week.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.50%, compared to 2.46% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.85%, versus 2.84% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Carolina Pica contributed to this report.) \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-04-11 1651GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110426e74q0016t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
