\par\par \b \uc2 Foreign bets push  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso to pre- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  highs\b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2011\par 20:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Foreign bets shift $2.2 bln in favor of peso in 1 month\par \par \uc2 * Peso at strongest since Jan. 3 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  launch\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, April 25 (Reuters) - Foreign bets on the Chilean peso's rally are at their strongest in two months, eroding the impact of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to near three-year highs, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Monday.\par \par \uc2 On the eve of the bank's dollar-buying program, the foreign position in Chilean non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) <CLPNDF=> represented a net $1.675 billion bet on a stronger peso <CLP=CL>, fueling a rally that squeezed exporters' margins.\par \par \uc2 Following the Jan. 3 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, investors unwound bets and covered themselves against the weakening peso, compounded by conflict in the Arab world, switching positions by mid-March to a net $3 billion bet on a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2 But from March 17 to April 20, a net $2.2 billion shift in \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NDF contracts back toward a long peso position -- the most\par bullish in two months -- suggested rising risk appetite has\par emboldened new foreign bets in favor of the peso.\par <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par > For a graphic, see           \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/hyp29r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/hyp29r}}}\uc2 \f2 \par > For more on NDFs, see                    [ID:nN04186082]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is a sign that foreign investors' bets in favor of the peso have increased, putting downward pressure on the dollar locally," said Osvaldo Cruz, a BCI analyst in Santiago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The shifting tide in the forward market may compound the effects of global dollar weakness, rising interest rates and the strong price of top export copper, which have nearly erased the initial 7 percent impact of the dollar-buying program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investment bank Bci said on Monday authorities may turn to micro or macro-prudential measures to tame the peso.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local authorities have not yet considered capital controls in the top copper producer, although in a newspaper interview published on Monday \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Enrique Marshall said those limits cannot be "completely ruled out."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso closed a shade weaker on Monday to bid 467.3 pesos per U.S. dollar after testing a 16-week intraday high of 466.5 per dollar -- a level last seen before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Moises Avila and Brad Haynes; Editing by Andrew Hay)\f28 \par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/NDF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110425e74p000wa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
