\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Higher, Track US Markets, Await Local Earnings\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2011\par 18:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended higher Thursday, in line with rising U.S. markets, as participants bought shares ahead of a long holiday weekend and the start of earnings season.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa gained 0.4% to 4738.66 points, while market volume fell to 48.0 billion Chilean pesos ($102.8 million), down from CLP85.6 billion the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The Santiago Stock Exchange closed early Thursday ahead of the long Easter weekend when many Chileans go on vacation. All markets and government offices will be closed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 As several of the Ipsa's heavier-weighted shares also trade in New York, the Ipsa often tracks the Dow Jones Industrial Average. In recent trading, the DJIA was up 29 points, or 0.2%, at 12483 as a round of robust earnings reports overshadowed lackluster U.S. economic data.\par \par \uc2 Among dually listed shares, flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN) climbed 0.9% to CLP12,740.00 after Chile's antitrust court set a May 26 date to hold a public hearing regarding a private consumer-rights group's petition filed against LAN's proposed merger with Brazil's TAM S/A (TAM, TAMM4.BR).\par \par \uc2 Additionally, chemical and specialty fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) grew 0.6% to CLP27,450.00 and power producer \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN) rose 1.0% to CLP864.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, with the first quarter earnings season scheduled to get under way next week and companies poised to post strong bottom lines on the back of firm demand and robust economic growth, the Ipsa rose.\par \par \uc2 "Although inflation is the rock in emerging nations' shoe, it won't hamper strong economic growth. Meanwhile, domestic demand is set to remain strong," said Ximena Garcia, head of studies at local brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 Inflation will likely end this year at 4.3%, above the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3%, plus/minus one percentage point.\par \par \uc2 Among other gainers, telecommunications operator Entel (ENTEL.SN) gained 2.8% to CLP8,750.00 and power holding company \uc2 Enersis\uc2  (ENI, ENERSIS.SN) rose 1.3% to CLP196.45.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended at its strongest level versus the dollar since a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was announced in early January, as the greenback slumped against its rivals and copper prices surged.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP466.50 to the dollar, versus Wednesday's close of CLP469, while trading in a range of CLP466.50 to CLP469.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP467.85 Thursday. It has accumulated $3.85 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed in light over-the-counter trading ahead of the long holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.44%, compared to 2.43% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 2.83%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 21-04-11 1656GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110421e74l001cm\par }\page {\par\fs2