\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Ends At Strongest Since  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  On Weak Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2011\par 17:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended Thursday at its strongest level versus the dollar since a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was announced in early January, as the greenback slumped against its rivals and copper prices surged.\par \par \uc2 The peso strengthened to CLP466.50 to the dollar, versus Wednesday's close of CLP469, while trading in a range of CLP466.50 to CLP469.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed early Thursday ahead of the long Easter weekend when many Chileans go on vacation. All markets and government offices will be closed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Broad dollar weakness, on a worsening U.S. fiscal outlook and monetary policy that is expected to remain loose for the foreseeable future, helped boost the Chilean peso.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of its exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the session, the euro jumped to a 16-month high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Also, as Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Spot copper in London trading grew 1.7% to $4.35948 a pound, according to Chile copper commission Cochilco, on the back of a softer dollar.\par \par \uc2 "All things--copper prices, euro, equity markets--pointed to a stronger peso," said Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 The peso, however, still faces strong resistance at current levels before it can strengthen to preintervention levels, Soto said.\par \par \uc2 As part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP467.85 Thursday. It has accumulated $3.85 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 (Peso quote provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 21-04-11 1547GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110421e74l0019t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
