\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Would Be Stronger Without  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2011\par 20:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (updates with additional comments on inflation and the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday reiterated that without its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso would be stronger in relation to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In early 2011, the bank announced a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was trading at near three-year highs.\par \par \uc2 In prepared remarks to Congress, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president Jose De Gregorio, added that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't had "a very large effect" on the peso's trading levels in relation to the dollar, the bank is satified with its daily dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 He noted that the peso's trading levels versus the dollar will likely depend on global tensions and events.\par \par \uc2 "If there's a rebound in industrialized economies, we should see the dollar firm somewhat," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that monetary policy currently faces challenges stemming from significant international inflationary pressures as a result of rising international fuel and food prices.\par \par \uc2 While these imported pressures will push inflation in Chile to end the year at 4.3%, above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 3%, plus/minus one percentage point, core inflation, which factors out fuel and food prices will remain relatively stable.\par \par \uc2 "Core inflation will hover at around the target level throughout the bank's [24-month] policy horizon," De Gregorio said in his speech.\par \par \uc2 The central banker added that higher fuel prices account for 70 basis points of the one percentage point increase in the higher headline inflation outlook.\par \par \uc2 Inflation, at least for two or three quarters, will gain past the higher end of the bank's tolerance range, but these increases will be transitory and limited.\par \par \uc2 He reiterated the bank will continue withdrawing its monetary stimulus to keep inflation in line.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased the benchmark rate a total 75 basis points, bringing it to 4%.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the benchmark rate to end the year around 5.5% to 6%. De Gregorio later noted this rate outlook was incorporated in the bank's baseline scenario for the year.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 04-04-11 1800GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110404e74400132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
