\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends 1.1% Stronger On Libya Ceasefire, G-7  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso ended 1.1% stronger versus the dollar Friday as market participants reacted to the Libyan government's ceasefire, the Group of Seven's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  agreement to weaken the yen and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bigger-than-expected rate increase.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP480.80 to the dollar, versus Thursday's close of CLP486.10, while trading in a range of CLP480.80 to CLP484.00.\par \par \uc2 Market participants breathed a sigh of relief on Libya's ceasefire and on the agreement for each G-7 country to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their own market.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are more at ease with Libya's ceasefire and a possible resolution to the violence in that country. Participants also kept a keen eye on the G-7's agreement to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen," said Rodrigo Sarria, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with investment bank Celfin Capital.\par \par \uc2 Also, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Thursday raised the benchmark overnight rate 50 basis points to 4%, surpassing market expectations for a quarter of a percentage point increase, making the peso more attractive for capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Friday, as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP481.75. It has accumulated $2.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended higher following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate increase.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.41%, from 2.39% Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.88%, from 2.87% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 18-03-11 1656GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i0017d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
