\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Chile peso surges on unexpectedly high rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 13:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Market expected smaller interest rate increase\par \par \uc2 * Japan, Mideast have given \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more room on peso\par \par \uc2 * Central banks omits mention of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in statement\par \par \uc2 (Updates with peso movement, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  release)\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, March 18 (Reuters) - Chile's peso <CLP=CL> gained nearly 1 percent on Friday a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its benchmark interest rate aggressively to fight rising inflationary pressures.\par \par \uc2 The bigger-than-expected 50-basis-point increase on Thursday evening brings Chile's benchmark rate <CLINTR=ECI> to 4 percent, raising the allure for foreign investors and boosting the peso's recovery from the impact of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program launched in January.\par \par \uc2 The steeper rate hike caught \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's market off guard, as a Reuters poll, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surveys and interest-rate futures had all pointed to a 25-basis-point increase. For more see [ID:nN15270164].\par \par \uc2 Traders quickly adjusted to a wider differential with near-zero interest rates in developed economies such as the United States and Japan, pushing the peso up more than 1 percent against the U.S. dollar in early trade before paring midday gains to 0.9 percent at 481.7 pesos to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The earthquake in Japan and unrest in the Arab world have helped to weaken the peso more than 3 percent from near three-year highs in February, reducing pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep rates low in the face of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.\par \par \uc2 The bank's Thursday release omitted reference to the peso for the first time since August. [ID:nN17171992]\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Brad Haynes; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-CHILE/PESO (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110318e73i000u8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
