\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Closes Weaker As Japan Nuclear Drama Unfolds\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended sharply weaker versus the dollar Tuesday as participants the world over watched the worst nuclear energy accident since Chernobyl unfold in quake-and-tsunami ravaged Japan.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP483.40 to the dollar, compared with CLP480.80 on Monday, while trading in a range of CLP483.20 to CLP486.60.\par \par \uc2 With investors fearing that the clock was quickly ticking down to avoid a full-blown disaster at Japan's troubled nuclear power plant, international copper prices dropped to their lowest level since mid-December and the safe-haven dollar rallied against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 "The peso's depreciation is completely due to the fallout from Japan's troubles...with investors shunning risk, the dollar is gaining, global markets are falling, as are commodities prices," said Nicolas de la Carrera, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader with \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP484.90. It has accumulated $2.5 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower following a scheduled auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -issued sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.45%, from 2.48% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.92%, from 2.99% the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 15-03-11 1656GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110315e73f001dc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
