\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank maintains pace of  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 126 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 20:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, March 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would maintain the pace of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the strong peso between March. 9 and April 8, and continue to buy $50 million of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily.\par \par \uc2 The peso, which weakened sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began in early January, has clawed back most of the 7 percent initially lost due to strong prices for the nation's main export copper and wider dollar weakness, and is again within striking distance of near three-year highs.\par \par \uc2 The government has ruled out capital controls, but markets are asking what additional steps, if any, the bank will take.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (URGENT)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110311e738001it\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
