\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Nearly Unchanged On Strong Jan Economic Growth\b0\par\par\uc2 By Renzo Dasso   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 18:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso closed practically unchanged against the dollar Monday, as stronger-than-expected local economic growth data offset lower international copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP473.50 compared with CLP473.90 on Friday, while trading in a range of CLP472.30 to CLP475.00.\par \par \uc2 The country's monthly economic activity index, or Imacec, grew 6.8% year-to-year in January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday. Growth surpassed the 6.0% increase market consensus had been expecting.\par \par \uc2 The positive figure boosted the peso amid falling copper prices due to the turmoil in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 The South American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  often takes direction from copper prices as Chile is the world's largest producer of the metal.\par \par \uc2 "What he have seen today are opposing forces at work. The Imacec figure was very good and held the peso amid the declines of copper, the U.S. dollar and stock markets abroad," said Ronald Volpi, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at local brokerage EuroAmerica.\par \par \uc2 Copper's losses deepened late Monday morning as the equities market fell on higher oil prices. The most actively traded contract, for May delivery, was recently down 3.7%, or 16.75 cents, at $4.3180 per pound on the Comex division of the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP472.70. It has accumulated $2.2 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the bank will announce it next round of market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank is expected to hold steady with its daily purchases of $50 million, despite the peso firming back to near pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, said Gloria Soto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower as the market awaits consumer price index data to be released before trading starts on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Consensus is for a 0.2% increase in the February CPI from the previous month.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.41%, from 2.47% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.94%, versus 2.97% on the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Renzo Dasso, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; renzo.dasso@dowjones.com [ 07-03-11 1729GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110307e7370015m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
