\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Closes Weaker, Erases Early Gains In Thin Session\b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolina Pica   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 17:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso closed weaker against the dollar Friday, erasing early gains after testing a significant resistance level.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at CLP473.90 compared with CLP472.80 on Thursday, while trading in a range of CLP471.40 to CLP474.20.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed when trading got underway on the stronger euro and the gains in London copper prices. It came up against the same resistance level it tested in late February amid near-record high copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile produces a third of the world's copper, its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes direction from the price of the metal.\par \par \uc2 "The peso hit resistance around the CLP471-CLP472 mark in early trading, but it didn't have the strength to break it," said Samuel Levy, analyst at ForexChile.\par \par \uc2 Volume was thinner than usual and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shrugged off comments from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president regarding market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Jose De Gregorio in prepared remarks said the peso would likely be trading 3% to 5% stronger with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, he reiterated that central banks, including \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's, should subordinate monetary policy to the concerns of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP472.34. It has accumulated $2.15 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed following the release the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting minutes.\par \par \uc2 The minutes show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't rule out speeding up the pace of its rate hikes later on in the year if inflationary pressures increase.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.47%, from 2.44% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 2.97%, unchanged from the previous session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 04-03-11 1656GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110304e73400112\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
