\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Pres: 2011  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Different From '08\b0\par\par\uc2 449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 14:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for this year has had a different effect than the bank's previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2008, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday in Paris.\par \par \uc2 Following the Jan. 3 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement, the peso initially weakened about 7% from the near three-year highs it was trading at. In recent weeks, however, it's recouped most of its strength.\par \par \uc2 "This contrasts sharply with the experience of the previous period of reserve accumulation initiated in April 2008," bank president Jose De Gregorio said in prepared remarks delivered at a symposium at the Bank of France.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio noted that in the 2008 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the peso depreciated by about 18% through late August and in the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the peso has even firmed to nearly the same levels before the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He attributed the different responses the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shown to the dollar's performance abroad and copper prices.\par \par \uc2 "In 2008, the dollar strengthened and the price of copper fell. Today, the dollar has remained weak and the copper price has reached all-time highs," he said.\par \par \uc2 Chile is the world's largest copper producer, mining roughly a third of global output, so its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes trading cues from the price of the red metal.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio, however, said that without the current \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 --which will increase \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves to 17% of gross domestic product--the peso would likely be trading 3% to 5% stronger from current levels.\par \par \uc2 He added than global exchange rate tensions will likely be transitory and will subside once industrialized economies recover from the current financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 De Gregorio noted that emerging economies are receiving capital inflows as a result of the cyclical differences between these and advanced economies, but that net capital inflows are below those seen in the early 1990s.\par \par \uc2 He added that Chile has not "seen net capital inflows yet."\par \par \uc2 Regarding monetary policy in emerging economies, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the main challenge for these economies is to avoid persistent deviations of inflation from its target, especially in light of rising prices for crude oil and agricultural commodities.\par \par \uc2 The risk of propagation to other prices has to be mitigated, he noted.\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy cannot be subordinated to exchange rate objectives, even in cases where measures to alleviate exchange rate appreciation have been adopted," De Gregorio said.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case, the sterilization of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through bond issues, allows monetary policy to retain its independence to stabilize inflation.\par \par \uc2 -By Carolina Pica, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8919; carolina.pica@dowjones.com [ 04-03-11 1300GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110304e734000u1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\sh