\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  stuck in ranges as oil weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2011\par 15:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulls real back from 2-month high\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso slips as concerns of high oil prices weigh\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso firms 0.19 pct, Brazil real 0.06 pct (New throughout, adds comments)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were trapped in narrow ranges Monday as investors remained cautious about the impact of higher oil prices on global growth and the region's importers, such as Chile.\par \par \uc2 Concerns that a spike in oil prices could hurt global growth have weighed on the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks, softening a trend of steady appreciation as investors are drawn to Latin America's relatively high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil prices rose above $112 a barrel, but the market calmed from last week's jumps as investors weighed a pledge of more supply from Saudi Arabia against the prospect of prolonged disruption to Libya's output.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of oil producers Mexico and Brazil managed to firm while the peso of Chile, an importer of crude, dipped.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico's peso has been strengthening since the peak of oil prices last week, so this is just unwinding these extreme scenarios on Middle East oil risk," said Igor Arsenin, head of Latin American fixed-income strategy at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "If we have a permanent increase in oil just because of lingering uncertainty in the Middle East, then it becomes actually favorable for oil exporters such as Mexico and less favorable for importers, countries like Chile," he added.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso firmed 0.19 percent to 12.1025 per dollar. Brazil's real bid 0.06 percent stronger on the local spot market to 1.661 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from a nearly two-month high hit early in the session by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  with two auctions to buy dollars in the spot market, a reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction and two dollar forward auctions.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso slipped 0.25 percent to 475.70 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Oil prices are more stable ... but the price is still near $112, which is very high for a country like ours that imports almost all of its petroleum," a Chilean trader said.\par \par \uc2 Investors pushed down yields on Brazilian interest rate futures on bets that government spending cuts may cool the need for an aggressive interest rate hike this week.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government said Monday it will slash spending on defense and low-income housing as part of $30 billion in cuts to this year's budget.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers meet Wednesday to decide on a possible hike in the country's interest rate.\par \par \uc2 While some market players were betting last week that they could raise rates by 75 basis points, the market began late last week to unwind those bets.\par \par \uc2 Yields on Mexican interest rate swaps edged up after the head of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expressed worry about crop failures from bad weather and said policymakers may have to raise interest rates if they poison inflation expectations.\par \par \uc2 Mexico, whose economic recovery has been slower than that of Brazil or Chile, has widely been expected not to raise interest rates until early in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico has been spared a significant pick-up in food inflation, but that could change purely because of local conditions," \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 's Arsenin said. (Additional reporting by Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo and Froilan Romero in Santiago; Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110303e72s00157\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
