\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2011\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ YAMAGUCHI: MUST WATCH INTERNATIONAL COMMODITY MARKET CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Hirohide Yamaguchi said Wednesday that the Japanese economy is returning to a gradual recovery as emerging countries lead the global rebound, but that caution is needed over recent rises in the price of commodities including oil amid mounting geopolitical tensions in the Middle East and North Africa. (published 0248 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SF FED OFFICIAL: MONETARY POLICY 'ACCOMMODATIVE' FOR EXTENDED PERIOD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The long recovery facing labor markets suggests the Federal Reserve will need to provide continued support to the economy for some time to come, a U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Tuesday. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBNZ: WORKING HARD TO ASSIST RECOVERY, ENSURE MARKETS REMAIN STABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand said Wednesday it is working hard to assist the recovery and ensure markets remain stable, after the 6.3 magnitude earthquake that struck New Zealand's second largest city just after midday Tuesday. (published 2349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN POSTS 1ST TRADE DEFICIT IN 22 MONTHS ON WEAK EXPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a rare trade deficit in January, as weaker-than-expected exports and a sharp increase in import costs pushed the numbers into the red for the first time in 22 months. (published 0055 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA FINANCE MINISTER: GLOBAL ECONOMIC CONDITIONS TURNING WORSE FOR DOMESTIC INFLATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Yoon Jeung-hyun said Wednesday the recent spike in prices of global oil and raw materials is negatively affecting the local economy by adding to increasing inflationary pressure. (published 0033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BANK OF THAILAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : INFLATION MANAGEABLE IN TARGET RANGE DESPITE HIGHER OIL PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  believes core inflation will remain manageable and within its target range for the year despite rising oil prices, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said late Tuesday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA'S STEVENS ARGUES FOR SAVINGS TO DEAL WITH INCOME SURGE INTO ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glenn Stevens\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Wednesday urged that savings growth continue as a means of allowing the domestic economy to deal with the mining investment boom, adding it is impossible to say how long the boom will last and that the economic expansions of China and India are unlikely to be short-lived. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA 4Q WAGE INDEX +1.0% ON QTR VS CONSENSUS +0.9% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian wages excluding bonuses rose a seasonally adjusted 1.0% in the fourth quarter of 2010 from the third quarter and rose 3.9% from a year earlier, Australian Bureau of Statistics labor price data issued Wednesday show. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN BUILDING ACTIVITY FALLS 5.1% IN 4Q VS 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The value of building work completed in Australia fell 5.1% to A$20.50 billion in the fourth quarter of 2010 from the third quarter, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said Wednesday. (published 0033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA & NZ BANKING GROUP PRICES DOLLAR BONDS TO YIELD 3.339% -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia & NZ Banking Group Ltd. priced the sale of its five-year global bond offering on Tuesday to yield 3.339%, according to a person familiar with the deal. (published 2246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: SENATE PANEL TO KICK OFF TAX CODE REVIEW NEXT WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Senate Finance Committee next week will embark on what is likely to be an exhaustive review of the U.S. tax code, as it hears from a quartet of former Treasury tax officials. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par POINT OF VIEW: GAINS IN US CONSUMER CONFIDENCE ALREADY CONSUMED BY EVENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the fast-paced financial market world, history gets started more quickly all the time. Feb. 10. Twelve days ago. History. So while enthusiasts for the growth of the U.S. economy surely want to take heart from the data on U.S. consumer confidence delivered earlier today by the Conference Board, the chilling reality is that date--Feb. 10. The Conference Board tells us in a press release: "The cutoff date for February's preliminary results was Feb. 10, 2011." (published 2205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BRAZILIAN REAL, CHILEAN PESO NEAR KEY PRE-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LEVELS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite ongoing efforts by Brazil's and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Chile\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's central banks to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, the Brazilian real and Chilean peso are defiantly approaching pre-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels, raising the question of whether these countries will make further efforts to curb them. (published 2323 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BRAZIL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FLEXES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MUSCLE IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market appeared ready to shrug off ongoing violence in North Africa and the Middle East on Tuesday, but a surprise reverse-swap auction by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a message of defiance from Libya was enough to undercut foreign-investment inflows. (published 2012 GMT) [ 23-02-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110223e72n0005b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
