\par\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Real, Chilean Peso Near Key Pre- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Levels\b0\par\par\uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2011\par 00:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely to ramp up \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  could provide trade entry point--money manager\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Erin McCarthy \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Despite ongoing efforts by Brazil's and Chile's central banks to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, the Brazilian real and Chilean peso are defiantly approaching pre-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels, raising the question of whether these countries will make further efforts to curb them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If central banks stand back, that could pave the way for more gains, but some strategists warn about the risks of more intense \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Both central banks have argued that their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be significantly stronger had they not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at all. But now rising inflation concerns have led both countries to raise interest rates recently, with more hikes expected this year, which only will encourage stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the future.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  nearing major psychological and technical breakthroughs, investors who are already long on either \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should stay in those positions for now, since there is room for further strength, said Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Scotland\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saw some losses on Tuesday from general risk aversion on Middle East worries, robust copper prices in Chile, the world's largest producer of the red metal, and strong capital inflows in Brazil have been key drivers of the peso's and real's strength in recent months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the real, reaching BRL1.65 to the dollar is a key psychological level that it could hit at "any time," while investors should watch for the peso to hit CLP466.70 to the dollar, Cattan-Naslausky said. If the real and peso do surpass those levels, investors could take profits before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are able to stabilize, she added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 John Peta, who manages an emerging-market, local-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond fund at Acadian Asset Management, said they remain overweight on the Brazilian real and Chilean peso.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We're long both \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because we think the fundamentals are quite positive," he said, adding that the high carry on the Brazilian real still makes it an attractive position. Already-high interest rates in Brazil and expected interest-rate increases in Chile should drive appreciation pressures, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, analysts say it's not a good time to enter into these trades, given their already-high valuations and further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Of the two, the real is riskier to buy right now, given Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ongoing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  efforts. It regularly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot, forward and futures markets. Most notably, in October, Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by twice raising its financial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tax on foreign purchases of local assets, in an effort to curb hot money inflows from abroad. Before that second tax hike, the real was near the BRL1.65 mark, which it is now approaching.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The threat of further measures in Brazil is a serious one, said Alberto Ramos, economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could intensify its current measures or it could also employ more unorthodox capital controls, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chilean peso, meanwhile, is more likely to be given some room to appreciate. In Chile, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced a $12 billion dollar purchasing program for the year in early January, after the peso gained more than 7% in 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But further action from Chile's traditionally conservative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is less likely, even though it could increase the amount of its daily dollar purchases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They are not ready to go to places that the Brazilians are ready to go," Ramos said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Andean nation's hawkish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 monetary authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has hinted at a shift in priorities, from curbing the peso to focusing on the inflation battle, given its 25-basis-point rate hike last week--making it more likely that the peso will strengthen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But if the two banks ultimately do \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it could provide a buying opportunity for these two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said Adnan Akant, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and managing director at money manager \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fischer Francis Trees & Watts\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a New York unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is just a way of cheapening them up for those who really want to be involved in them," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Currently the money manager is not exposed to the Chilean peso or the Brazilian real, after pulling out of a long-real position last year on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Given the recent bout of risk aversion on Middle East concerns, it's "wait-and-see" whether global markets stabilize, but if any new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaken the two \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it could provide an advantageous entry point, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Erin McCarthy, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2712; erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com [ 02-22-11 1823ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110222e72m00132\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
