\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End Lower For 4th Straight Day As Investors Sell\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2011\par 21:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's blue-chip Ipsa index ended lower Friday for a fourth consecutive session as investors continued to cash in shares in favor of U.S. and European equity.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa closed 0.7% lower at 4445.98 points, while volume rose to 70.3 billion Chilean pesos ($150.2 million) from CLP69.6 billion the prior session.\par \par \uc2 In all, the Ipsa has lost nearly 10% since December as investors migrate to U.S. and European shares in search of better returns.\par \par \uc2 "There's been a reshuffling of global investment portfolios, from emerging markets to more developed markets," said Pablo Andalaft, head of investment strategy at local brokerage Negocios y Valores Corredora de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 After the Ipsa's 37.6% surge last year many participants viewed local equity as pricey, but the recent drop may be bringing share prices to attractive levels again.\par \par \uc2 "Prices are much more reasonable now after the Ipsa's recent losses," said Andalaft, adding that with strong fundamentals there is plenty of upside potential.\par \par \uc2 Select-shares which had posted the biggest gains last year, were again among the session's biggest decliners.\par \par \uc2 Flagship carrier \uc2 LAN Airlines\uc2  (LFL, LAN.SN), whose merger with Brazilian airline \uc2 TAM SA\uc2  (TAM, TAMM4.BR) was recently put on hold by the Chilean antitrust court, fell 1.0% to CLP13,303.00.\par \par \uc2 Also, Chile's largest construction company, \uc2 SalfaCorp\uc2  (SALFACORP.SN), declined 2.5% to CLP1,530.30; specialty chemical and fertilizer producer SQM's (SQM) more liquid B-series (SQM-B.SN) lost 2.2% to CLP25,575.00 and retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) shed 1.5% to CLP3,132.10.\par \par \uc2 In other local markets, the peso ended stronger against the dollar--inching closer to an almost three-year high despite a continuing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program--on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate increase and the euro's gains versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP468.40, compared with CLP469.70 Thursday, while trading in a range of CLP468.40 to CLP470.40.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP468.71. It has accumulated $1.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.67%, from 2.64% Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 3.14%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 18-02-11 2033GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110218e72i0017c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
