\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Stronger On Rate Rise, Euro's Gains Vs Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2011\par 17:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended stronger against the dollar--inching closer to an almost three-year high despite a continuing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program--on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate increase and the euro's gains versus the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP468.40, compared with CLP469.70 on Thursday, while trading in a range of CLP468.40 to CLP470.40.\par \par \uc2 After the market closed in the prior session, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its benchmark overnight rate by a quarter of a percentage point, as expected, to 3.5%.\par \par \uc2 Interest-rate increases tend to foster capital inflows, as participants seek better returns.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, the peso strengthened as the euro rallied against the dollar after hawkish comments from a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  executive board member.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly export-dependent and nearly a third of its exports are bound for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP468.71. It has accumulated $1.65 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The peso has pared back its post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses on record-high copper prices--which it tracks because Chile is the world's premier producer of the metal--robust economic growth and expectations for continued interest-rate increases.\par \par \uc2 "If the dollar remains under pressure next week and copper prices continue gaining, we could see the peso breach its pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels...although it probably would stabilize at that level," said Sergio Tricio, head of studies at local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chile.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.67%, from 2.64% on Thursday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 3.14%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 18-02-11 1657GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110218e72i0014d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
