\par\par \b \uc2 SCENARIOS-Options to tame  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2011\par 23:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Widening rates differential attracts dollars\par \par \uc2 * Peso has nearly recovered from post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drop\par \par \uc2 * Government reiterates not considering capital controls\par \par \uc2 By Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday reduced options to tame a strong peso hammering exporters when it raised its benchmark rate <CLINTR=ECI> by 25 basis points to 3.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 (For the main story, see [ID:nN17302923])\par \par \uc2 The bank made inflation worries a priority and in doing so likely added upward pressure to the peso <CLP=CL>.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trading near 3-year highs despite a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , boosted by strong prices for main export copper and wider dollar weakness.\par \par \uc2 (For a graphic, see: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/jud77r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/jud77r}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Felipe Larrain reiterated earlier on Thursday that Chile is not interested in the sort of secondary measures implemented by Brazil and Peru to address the capital flows behind their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' strength.\par \par \uc2 An aversion to unorthodox \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures and the mounting costs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have left Chilean authorities with a sparse second line of defense to bolster their battle against the peso's export-damaging climb.\par \par \uc2 "They've been burning their boats, bit by bit," said BCI economist Luis Felipe Alarcon.\par \par \uc2 The following are some possible scenarios:\par \par \uc2 MORE LIKELY:\par \par \uc2 * A public commitment to invest the state's dollar revenues in a sovereign wealth fund overseas rather than spending them in the local economy would boost market certainty about the government's commitment to a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2 Economic growth, forecast at over 5 percent both this year and last, will boost Chile's tax revenue in pesos and let the government rely less on dollars from state miner Codelco's copper exports.\par \par \uc2 * The government could also allow companies to pay taxes in dollars, relieving demand for pesos from businesses with foreign revenues. Traders said the peso's 0.9 percent rise on Thursday was driven by mining companies selling dollars on the local market to pay monthly taxes denominated in pesos.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has left open the chance to increase the volume of its daily $50 million dollar purchases once the second phase of the program ends on March 8. [ID:nSAG002719]\par \par \uc2 Raising the volume of the daily auctions to $75 million or $100 million would speed up the pace of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and increase market certainty that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy the full $12 billion it pledged to accumulate this year.\par \par \uc2 * Capital market reforms pending congressional approval include a measure giving regulators more discretion to set hedging requirements for pension funds' overseas investments.\par \par \uc2 The pension funds are currently required by law to hedge at least 50 to 85 percent of their foreign portfolios, diminishing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of their investments abroad, which make up more than $67 billion of nearly $150 billion under management.\par \par \uc2 Looser hedging requirements could eventually magnify the effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's November decision to let the privately managed pension funds invest more abroad. [ID:nN15266330] [ID:nN10214819]\par \par \uc2 LESS LIKELY\par \par \uc2 * Analysts also see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unwilling to increase the total scale of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the record $12 billion in dollar purchases announced on Jan. 3.\par \par \uc2 Yields on 10-year \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds <CLBCU10Y=RR> have risen nearly 20 basis points to 3.15 percent since the bank announced it would sterilize, or offset, its dollar auctions by issuing debt, magnifying the financial cost of the program.\par \par \uc2 * Shifting some of the bank's dollar purchases into the derivatives market via non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) would reduce the cost of sterilizing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would mean giving up the accumulation of actual reserves.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the principal objective of its dollar auctions was to grow its foreign reserves to levels comparable with regional peers, and the bank may be hesitant to undermine its credibility by shifting strategies. (Editing by Simon Gardner; Editing by Andrew Hay)\par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/ (SCENARIOS)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|C|GRO|MTL|SOF|RNP|PCM   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110217e72h001qy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
