\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 6-Chile raises key rate 25 bps despite strong peso\b0\par\par\uc2 792 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2011\par 22:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raises key rate by 25 basis points\par \par \uc2 * Bank suggests more rate hikes are coming\par \par \uc2 * Quickening inflation is bank's principal concern\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  peso nears pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, stocks fall\par \par \uc2 (Updates with fresh economist comment)\par \par \uc2 By Simon Gardner and Brad Haynes\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Reuters) - Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday raised its benchmark interest rate and signaled more hikes were on the way as it prioritizes inflation worries over its concerns about a strong peso that is hammering exporters.\par \par \uc2 The 25-basis-point hike to 3.5 percent, which had been widely expected, will probably put more pressure on the peso, \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which has risen with prices for Chile's main export -- copper\par -- and widening dollar weakness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso is trading near three-year highs despite a $12 billion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market in January by holding rates steady after seven straight increases to complement the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But investors now see annual inflation at 4.0 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in December -- the upper limit of a 2 percent to 4\par percent target range -- prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to act.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As in regional powerhouse Brazil, inflation in Chile quickened in January, driven partly by rising fuel prices. That put pressure on central bankers to follow the lead of a host of emerging market economies from China to India and Thailand to Peru raising rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Widening differentials with near-zero interest rates in economies such as the United States and Japan have prompted investors to seek higher returns in markets like Brazil and Chile.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cited higher market near-term inflation expectations, but said prices had behaved as expected and core inflation was limited. It also said it would continue to withdraw monetary stimulus in coming months, signaling more hikes to come.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The strong increase in inflation expectations, due to rising energy and food prices, as well as lower unemployment and the dynamism of internal demand, were the main factors that triggered this decision," said Matias Madrid, chief economist at Banco Penta in Santiago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Going forward, we expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to continue increasing the rate gradually but continually during the first half of the year, and we will only see pauses in the second half," he said.25-basis-point increase, while 16 of 20 analysts polled by Reuters were betting on it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chile's peso closed 0.87 percent firmer earlier on Thursday, nearing pre-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels. Chilean stocks closed 1.3 percent lower as investors fled equities for domestic bonds on expectations of a hike. Yields on five-year inflation-indexed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds have fallen 10 basis points this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chilean consumer prices rose 0.3 percent in January, in line with market forecasts, government data showed last week, boosting bets the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would raise its key rate. Core CPI, which strips out prices for fuel, fresh fruit and vegetables, rose 0.1 percent in January.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Both the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the government are doing all we can to contain inflationary pressures," Finance Minister Felipe Larrain told reporters on Thursday, reiterating that the government was not considering capital controls. "We must be clear that some of those inflationary pressures are coming from international prices."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exporters, whose revenues have fallen in peso terms as the dollar weakens, have publicly called on the government to take measures to sap the peso's strength.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jose De Gregorio said Sunday it is vital to control inflation, given rising global oil and food prices. That sent a strong signal that inflation was the bank's overriding focus.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There are a lot of references to inflation in the bank's rate statement and nothing about the peso," said Erwin Andia, director of Santiago-based brokerage \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chile. "The dollar will open weaker (against the peso Friday) and that trend should continue."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't see the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the very near-term," he added. "It is conscious it can't change the dollar's (downward) trend, because it is an international phenomenon," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank said on Wednesday the peso's rise since hitting a trough in late 2008 was "not very different" from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains in other commodity exporters and emerging markets where there had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets are asking what additional steps, if any, the bank and the government will take. De Gregorio on Sunday stressed that any controls to counter \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation should be carefully studied.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso weakened sharply after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began in early January, but has been boosted since by strong copper prices and wider dollar weakness, clawing back much of the 7 percent initially lost.\f28 \par \par \uc2 CHILE-RATES/ (UPDATE 6, GRAPHIC)|LANGEN|Table|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110217e72h001oo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
