\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Sharply Stronger As Market Bets On Rate Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 424 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2011\par 18:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso ended sharply stronger versus the dollar Thursday, as market participants widely expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates by 25 basis points after market close.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP469.70 to the dollar, nearing an almost three-year high despite an ongoing $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, compared with CLP473.70 on Wednesday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded in a range of CLP470.00 to CLP475.00.\par \par \uc2 Deteriorating inflation expectations, which have in part been fueled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, will likely lead the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to more aggressive rate increases this year, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 In January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paused its interest-rate increases for the first time since starting to remove its massive monetary stimulus in June 2009. Participants speculated that the bank held the rate in January to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jose De Gregorio recently underscored that the bank's main goal is controlling inflation, a message participants interpreted to mean that meeting the inflation target won't be subjugated to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 "The market is betting on rates being increased. That would add pressure for the peso to strengthen even more as the gap between U.S. and Chilean rates would be greater," said Guillermo Kautz, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at local brokerage BCI Corredor de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 Interest-rate increases tend to foster capital inflows, as participants seek better returns.\par \par \uc2 Dollar sales by Chile's private pension-fund managers, or AFPs, also helped to fuel the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 "During the session we saw a lot of institutional dollar sales, especially by AFPs," Kautz said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP474.24. It has accumulated $1.60 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower on strong demand for bonds.\par \par \uc2 "AFPs have been selling dollars on the local market to buy fixed-income instruments," Kautz said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.64%, from 2.66% on Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.14%, from 3.16% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 17-02-11 1708GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110217e72h0019z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
