\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Weaker After Hitting Resistance, Dollar Purchases\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2011\par 17:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended sharply weaker versus the dollar Tuesday, bouncing back from its earlier gains after hitting resistance, as investors bought dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP472.40 to the dollar, compared with CLP469.30 on Monday. It traded in a range of CLP467.80 to CLP472.90.\par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the peso strengthened to within striking distance of levels not seen since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program in early January, but pared back those gains as investors began snapping up dollars.\par \par \uc2 "The peso hit resistance at CLP468 and at that point investors came out buying dollars," said Gloria Soto, head \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at FXCM Chile.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several weeks, the peso has pared back most of its post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses on rising international copper prices, expectations for robust domestic growth and anticipations for continued rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 As Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Also, interest rate hikes tend to foster capital inflows, as participants seek better returns.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP472.67. It has accumulated $1.50 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended slightly higher after a scheduled auction of 10-year BCUs, a local fixed-income trader said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds at 2.71%, from 2.70% on Monday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.22%, from 3.19% the prior session.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 15-02-11 1654GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110215e72f00175\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
