\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Stronger On Dollar Sales; Mostly Ignores Egypt\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2011\par 18:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's peso ended stronger versus the dollar Friday, mostly ignoring Egyptian President Hosni Mubarak's resignation, as banks and the nation's private pension fund managers sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP472.10 to the dollar, its strongest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program in early January, compared with CLP473.30 on Thursday. It traded in a range of CLP472.10 to CLP474.70.\par \par \uc2 Local private pension fund managers, or AFPs, and banks fueled the peso's strength as they sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 "AFPs continued to sell dollars, triggering banks' stop-loss selling orders, which further boosted the peso," said Felipe Herrera, trader with local brokerage EuroAmerica\par \par \uc2 Chile's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't react much to Mubarak's resignation following nearly three weeks of intense domestic and international pressure, despite the euro's knee-jerk reaction to the news. The peso often moves in the same direction as the euro does against the dollar as nearly a third of Chile's exports are bound for European ports.\par \par \uc2 "The peso really didn't move much on the news," said Herrera.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP473.43. It has accumulated $1.40 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended unchanged on the day in light over-the-counter trading.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended flat at 2.68%, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 3.19%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 11-02-11 1700GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110211e72b00149\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
