\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Chile peso firms to over 1-mo high, Brazil dips\b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2011\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2  bets backed by rate view, lower \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks\par \par \uc2 * Real slumps from more than one-month high\par \par \uc2 * Mexican finance minister rules out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real slumps 0.6 pct, Mexico peso flat\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle and Ana Nicolaci da Costa\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO (Reuters) - Chile's peso hit its strongest level in more than a month Thursday after a poll backed bets of higher interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks were seen receding, while Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen raising its benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 3.50 percent next week, according to a poll.\par \par \uc2 Chilean policymakers held borrowing costs steady last month to try to discourage yield-hungry investors from pouring into its assets. The pause complemented a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program introduced at the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 But the move spooked bond investors, who fear the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not doing enough to tame rising inflation. Now policymakers appear to be changing course.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held back from expanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program this week despite solid gains in the peso.\par \par \uc2 "People feel more comfortable that they will tolerate a stronger peso, because they need to worry about inflation," said Igor Arsenin, head of Latin American debt strategy at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Seven straight rate hikes last year drove the Chilean peso to a nearly three-year high, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy $50 million a day to help protect local exporters.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso bid 0.57 percent stronger to 473.50 per dollar, its strongest since early January. The peso has clawed back more than 5 percent from a 7 percent loss spurred by news of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early January.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real shed 0.6 percent to 1.669 per dollar, pulling back sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a more than one-month high in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 A broadly stronger dollar and a slump in the euro, a key proxy for gauging demand for riskier assets like emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , weighed on the real and Mexico's peso.\par \par \uc2 NO MEXICAN MEDDLING\par \par \uc2 Brazil's government unveiled budget cuts of about $30 billion Wednesday in a bid to regain credibility among investors worried that overspending is driving inflation higher and beyond the control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday we had a positive economic context here, especially with the announcement of the budget cuts, it makes Brazil seem more trustworthy ... so the day after it is normal that you have an adjustment," said Andre Sacconato, economist at Tendencias consultancy in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has been waging an even more intense battle than Chile to contain the strength of the real, which is considered one of the most overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world.\par \par \uc2 Brazil offers among the highest interest rates available, and a relentless flow of funds from global investors continues to bode further strength despite heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction Thursday, though the real did not react noticeably to the news.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso reversed steep early losses to trade flat at 12.0765 per dollar after Mexico's finance minister said the country will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, brushing off complaints from exporters who want a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has lagged the gains in other emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , giving policymakers more room to stay on the sidelines.\par \par \uc2 But some had begun to bet Mexico could follow suit with greater \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the peso gained around 4 percent since November to hit a nearly 2-1/2 year high last month. (Editing by Dan Grebler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|FUN    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110213e72a00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
