\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Stocks End 1.0% Higher, Rebound On Bargain Buying\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2011\par 21:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Chile's Ipsa blue-chip stock index ended 1.0% higher Thursday, rebounding from a sharp drop earlier in the session as investors went bargain hunting.\par \par \uc2 The Ipsa rose to 4475.04, while volume fell to 131.3 billion Chilean pesos ($277.4 million), compared to CLP184.8 billion the prior session. The Ipsa was down more than 1% earlier Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Considering the Ipsa's more-than 10% in losses so far this year, as participants cashed in shares to invest in U.S. and European equity, local shares are at a discount, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Traders have also maintained, however, that the Ipsa's recent slump was expected, albeit excessive, following its 37.6% surge last year.\par \par \uc2 "Following so many sessions of continued declines, participants felt that share prices had been punished too harshly and that prices were attractive," said Rodolfo Araneda, analysts at local brokerage Tanner.\par \par \uc2 Retailers, which were among the biggest decliners in recent weeks, jumped higher.\par \par \uc2 Retail holding giant \uc2 Cencosud\uc2  (CENCOSUD.SN) rose 4.1% to CLP3,199.90, the nation's largest department store, Falabella (FALABELLA.SN), increased 2.1% to CLP4,744.90 and retailer Ripley (RIPLEY.SN) grew 4.4% to CLP590.00.\par \par \uc2 Real-estate and construction companies also recovered from their earlier losses.\par \par \uc2 Chile's largest construction company, \uc2 SalfaCorp\uc2  (SALFACORP.SN), expanded 1.7% to CLP1,570.00, while real estate developer Paz (PAZ.SN) jumped 3.5% to CLP525.00\par \par \uc2 Power generators, which had reeled after the government the prior session announced measures to avoid blackouts as a drought continues to cut into hydroelectric power generation, also recovered from their slump.\par \par \uc2 The government's measures may include prohibiting generators from using water in reservoirs so that water can be used by midyear if the drought doesn't let up and reducing voltage by 5% to 10%.\par \par \uc2 Within the sector, the nation's largest power generator, \uc2 Endesa\uc2  (EOC, ENDESA.SN), rose 1.6% to CLP800.00, while rival generator \uc2 Colbun (COLBUN.SN) \uc2 leapt 2.9% to CLP116.38.\par \par \uc2 In other market news, the peso ended stronger versus the dollar, after breaking a technical level of resistance, as Chile's private pension fund managers sold dollars.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP473.30 to the dollar, its strongest level since a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program was announced in early January, compared to CLP476.10 on Wednesday. It traded in a range of CLP473.30 to CLP478.15.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP478.08. It has accumulated $1.35 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed after 35 local analysts polled in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest monthly economic outlook saw the consumer price index likely gaining 4.0% in 2011 on the year.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees inflation gaining 3.3% this year, according to its last forecast.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.68%, from 2.67% Wednesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed unchanged at 3.19%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com [ 10-02-11 2030GMT ]\par \par \uc2 5057   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110210e72a001qx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
