\par\par \b \uc2 Chile Peso Ends Stronger;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Keeps $50M Daily Buys\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcela Castro   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2011\par 18:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso closed stronger versus the dollar on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed late the previous session that it will continue buying $50 million daily through March as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP476.10 to the dollar, its strongest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was announced in early January, compared to CLP478.90 on Tuesday. It traded in a range of CLP476.10 to CLP478.70.\par \par \uc2 On Jan. 5, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to stem the peso's significant appreciation. During the program's first phase, which ended Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million a day.\par \par \uc2 Market participants had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase its daily dollar purchases to $75 million or $100 million for the next 30 days as the peso pared back most of its losses against the dollar since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased $50 million at an average rate of CLP477.15. It has accumulated $1.30 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed its [daily] dollar purchases will continue to be $50 million and that was the main driver today for the peso's strength," said Sebastian Momberg, trader at local investment bank BCI.\par \par \uc2 Rising international copper prices and the euro's gains against the dollar, also boosted the peso.\par \par \uc2 Spot copper prices in London rose 0.7% to $4.53592 a pound, according to Chile's state copper commission Cochilco, after falling sharply the previous session on China's interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually look at Cochilco's daily market report for copper price data.\par \par \uc2 As Chile's economy is highly dependent on exports and nearly a third of them are destined for European ports, the peso often moves in the same direction the euro does against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro gained early versus the dollar as Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke reiterated his concerns about the strength of the U.S. economy while playing down inflation concerns.\par \par \uc2 "The euro's rally also helped the peso's strength today," added Momberg.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended mixed as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published Feb. 9- Mar. 8 sovereign debt auction schedule.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended at 2.67% from 2.57% Tuesday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.19% from 3.20%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Marcela Castro, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8908; marcela.castro@dowjones.com [ 09-02-11 1746GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110209e729001kw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
