\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  cenbank to maintain  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  pace\b0\par\par\uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2011\par 20:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO, Feb 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would maintain the pace of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the strong peso between Feb. 9 and March 8, and continue to buy $50 million of U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  daily.\par \par \uc2  The peso, which weakened sharply after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began in early January, has clawed back more than half of the 7 percent initially lost due to strong prices for main export copper and wider dollar weakness, and is again within striking distance of near three-year highs.\par \par \uc2  The government has ruled out capital controls, but markets are asking what additional steps, if any, the bank will take. For details, see [ID:nN31202514]  (Reporting by Moises Avila)  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110208e728001j1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
