\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  Peso Stays Strong; Views Of Greater  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Grow\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anthony Esposito   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 19:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--Faced with a stubbornly strong peso, the Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may increase the daily dollar purchases of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program to $75 million or $100 million from a current $50 million per day, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Following the peso's significant appreciation last year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local market through sterilized dollar purchases totaling $12 billion this year.\par \par \uc2 While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already accumulated $1.2 billion during the first phase of its program, which started Jan. 5 and is scheduled to end on Feb. 9, increasing daily dollar purchases should help to stem the peso's continued gains.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should consider using bigger bullets," by making more aggressive daily dollar purchases, Felipe Alarcon, deputy head of research at local investment bank BCI, wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The peso weakened some 7% to near CLP500 in the week following the program's announcement. It has since regained most of its losses on the back of record-high copper prices and deteriorating inflation expectations, which likely anticipate more interest rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the economy.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, deteriorating inflation expectations, in part due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program itself, are expected to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue hiking interest rates. This will make returns on capital inflows more attractive and tend to appreciate the peso further.\par \par \uc2 The peso's sizable appreciation last year helped keep inflation benign, absorbing most increases in import prices, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program has taken that cushion away.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the benchmark overnight rate at 3.25% in January, its first pause since it started removing its massive monetary stimulus in June last year.\par \par \uc2 "The effects [of the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and depreciation] were still too new to reach conclusions on where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would move to and on its inflationary consequences," the minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's January monetary policy meeting said.\par \par \uc2 Considering that inflation expectations are rising, however, participants anticipate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue tightening monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "We don't expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to risk falling behind on the inflation front by turning more dovish to curtail \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation," \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 Not all participants are convinced that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its daily dollar purchases, however, as the bank's accompanying bond-buying sterilization program has already fueled bond yield increases. Higher yields typically fuel more capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to sterilize the dollar purchases more quickly if it increased [the purchases] to $75 million and that would push bond yields even higher...I'm not sure the bank would want to do that," said Nathan Pincheira, fixed-income analyst with local investment bank Banchile Inversiones.\par \par \uc2 -By Anthony Esposito, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8929; anthony.esposito@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.) [ 07-02-11 1852GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110207e727001bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
