\par\par \b \uc2 Chile's Peso Closes Weaker Despite Record High Copper Prices\b0\par\par\uc2 By Marcela Castro   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 18:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO (Dow Jones)--The Chilean peso closed slightly weaker versus the U.S. dollar Monday, shrugging off copper hitting a new record high on international markets.\par \par \uc2 The peso ended at CLP479.50 to the dollar compared to CLP478.70 on Friday, after trading in a range of CLP477.30 to CLP479.80.\par \par \uc2 Spot copper prices in London rose 1.6% to $4.60170 a pound, according to Chile's state copper commission Cochilco, buoyed by last week's raft of positive economic news from the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Because Chile is the world's largest copper producer and exporter, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market participants usually keep an eye on New York and London copper prices to gauge export revenue inflows and the general health of the Chilean economy.\par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the peso firmed on the copper-price high, but retreated towards its closing price in later trading as volume thinned out.\par \par \uc2 Market volumes in February, the southern-hemisphere month when Chileans traditionally go on summer holidays, tend to be lower than usual.\par \par \uc2 "The market has been depressed in terms of volume. Resistance remains at CLP476-478 and support at CLP498-CLP500. The record copper price has been the major factor behind the peso's strength [in recent months]," \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader Gloria Soto at FXCM Chile said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Chile\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program for 2011, purchased $50 million on the local market on Monday at an average rate of CLP477.33. It has accumulated $1.2 billion so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The program's first phase ends Feb. 9 and market participants believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may increase its daily dollar purchases to $75 million or $100 million in the program's next phase.\par \par \uc2 In the bond market, yields on inflation-indexed Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, or BCUs, ended lower as the market awaits January inflation data to be released Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect the consumer-price index to gain 0.3% on the month.\par \par \uc2 The yield on five-year BCU bonds ended lower at 2.61% from 2.67% on Friday, while the yield on 10-year BCUs closed at 3.17%, from 3.19%.\par \par \uc2 (Peso and bond quotes provided by Valor Futuro newswire.)\par \par \uc2 -By Marcela Castro, Dow Jones Newswires; 56-2-715-8908;\par \par \uc2 marcela.castro@dowjones.com [ 07-02-11 1744GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1170 1844   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110207e727001at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
