\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Bets on  \highlight22\uc2 Chile \highlight\uc2  peso undercut  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  impact\b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2011\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Foreigners renew forward bets unwound post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Derivatives compound fundamentals driving peso strength\par \par \uc2 * NDF bets diluting impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Moises Avila\par \par \uc2 SANTIAGO, Feb 4 (Reuters) - Foreign bets on the Chilean peso's appreciation are recovering strength in the local derivatives market, eroding the impact of a $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  early last month.\par \par \uc2 The shifting tide in the forward market may compound the effects of global dollar weakness, rising interest rates and the record price of top export copper, which have halved the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in under a month.\par \par \uc2 On the eve of the bank's dollar-buying program, the foreign position in Chilean non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) <CLPNDF=> represented a net $1.675 billion bet on a stronger peso <CLP=CL>, helping to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to near 3-year highs.\par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Jan. 3 announcement, investors quickly unwound bets and covered themselves against the depreciating peso, shifting their positions by Jan. 20 to a net $2.111 billion bet on a weaker peso.\par \par \uc2 But by Feb. 2, a net $522 million shift in NDF contracts back to a long peso position suggested foreign investors see the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's downside risk subsiding as the exchange rate erases over one-half of its 7 percent post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  swing.\par \par \uc2 "There's now a recovery (in the forwards market), with new bets coming out in favor of the peso," said analyst Osvaldo Cruz of Chilean bank BCI. "It's complicating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , essentially producing an appreciative effect and therefore offsetting part of the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   > For a graphic, see            \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/vuc87r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/vuc87r }}}\uc2 \f2 \par   > For a TAKE-A-LOOK, see                   [ID:nN30113748]\par   > SCENARIOS-Remaining options to tame peso [ID:nN31202514]\par   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data showed the net shift in foreigners' forward positions over the past nine sessions is equivalent to more than 10 of the bank's daily $50 million dollar auctions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daily trade in Chile's NDF market averages about $350 million to $400 million, about one-third the size of the country's daily spot market and one-tenth the scale of forwards trade in regional powerhouse Brazil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NDFs are forward peso derivatives that investors use to hedge other investments against exchange rate risk or to openly speculate on a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Derivatives trading can impact the daily exchange rate when local banks cover their forward contracts by buying or selling dollars in the spot market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a NDF trade, investors either gain or lose the difference between the spot exchange rate and their bet, without handing over the underlying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market is betting with forwards that the local supply of dollars will strengthen the peso, maybe even to pre-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels," said one New York-based NDF trader, asking not to be named in line with company policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso has also been helped by economic fundamentals as copper export revenues reached record highs and foreign investment helps fuel Chile's bounding economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market inflation forecasts have risen to the upper limit of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's annual target, reinforcing expectations the bank will raise its benchmark interest rate next Thursday for the eighth time in nine months. For details, see [ID:nSAG002696]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chile has ruled out limiting capital inflows that chase higher yields in emerging markets, breaking ranks with regional peers like Brazil and reducing its policy arsenal for confronting the peso's rally. [ID:nN31202514]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's remaining options on the exchange rate is an increase to the volume of its daily dollar auctions after the first phase of the program ends on Feb. 9. [ID:nN03137860] (Reporting by Alonso Soto; writing by Brad Haynes; editing by Simon Gardner and Jeffrey Benkoe)\f28 \par \par \uc2 CHILE-PESO/NDF (ANALYSIS, GRAPHIC)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|D|M   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110207e7240013p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
