\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Chile industry output seen up 3.9 pct in December\b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2011\par 19:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WHAT: Chile industrial output for December\par \par \uc2 WHEN: Friday, Jan. 28 at 9 a.m. local time (1200 GMT)\par \par \uc2 REUTERS FORECAST: Industrial output <CLIP=ECI> is seen rising 3.9 percent in December from a year ago, according to a Reuters poll of eight analysts and economists.\par \par \uc2 The forecast is an increase from November's 2.5 percent year-on-year expansion and would help lift industrial output by 0.8 percent in 2010 from 2009.\par \par \uc2 FACTORS TO WATCH: Strong growth is seen as the result of rising sales overseas along with healthy domestic demand in the world's top copper producer.\par \par \uc2 Chile's exports <CLEXP=ECI> rose to a record $7.4 billion in December, contributing to the peso's <CLP=CL> 17-percent appreciation in the second half of last year.\par \par \uc2 MARKET IMPACT: Robust industrial data could stoke rising inflation expectations, as higher global food and commodity prices raise concerns after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held its benchmark interest rate this month following seven straight increases.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate futures show the market expects the bank to raise its key rate <CLINTR=ECI> by 25 basis points next month to 3.5 percent, providing further support for an appreciating peso despite the bank's $12 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Maria Jose Latorre; Editing by Padraic Cassidy)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CHILE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -ECONOMY/OUTPUT (PREVIEW)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|D|M|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110125e71p002dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
